    "created_at": "2016-01-08T23:35:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-08T23:35:20Z",
    "body": "Good question. I would lean toward a PrintTable function. The job of the algorithm is probably mostly taken up by validation and filtering out things not in the properties argument; it then passes the result on to PrintTable.\n\nI guess another big part of the algorithm will be converting from the passed JS object, to the internal spec Record type that represents a table. This is important because this is where you say the exact behavior for e.g. in what order getters get called, or whether you do prototype lookups, or similar. I would suspect existing implementations _might_ use their Web IDL bindings (which have \"dictionary\" conversion functionality) for this, but I am not sure. There are questions like e.g. if something is filtered out, do implementations call the getter anyway?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
